<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="biostats-notes-7-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title> Linear Regression </title>
    
    <objectives>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Students will be able to...
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <ol>
            <li><p> Sketch scatterplots for bivariate data </p></li>
            <li><p> Find the equation of the regression line for bivariate data </p></li>
        </ol>
    </objectives>

    <definition xml:id="def-bivariate">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Data that comes from two populations is called <alert>bivariate</alert>. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <definition xml:id="def-scatterplot">
        <statement>
            <p>
                A <alert>scatterplot</alert> is a graph that displays bivariate data.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <example>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Activity 16 problem 2a
            </p>
        </statement>
    </example>

    <p>
        Scatterplots can suggest relationships between variables. When we suspect a linear relationship, we can perform <alert>linear regresison</alert> to find a line of best fit for the data. 
    </p>

    <definition xml:id="def-least-squares-error">
        <statement>
            <p>
                The <alert>Least-Squares Error (LSE)</alert> between <m>X</m> and <m>Y</m> is <md>S_{XY} = \sum_{i}^n (x_i - \bar{x})(y_i - \bar{y})</md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <example>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Activity 16 problem 2b
            </p>
        </statement>
    </example>

    <definition xml:id="def-regression-line">
        <statement>
            <p>
                The <alert>regression line</alert> between <m>X</m> and <m>Y</m> is <md> y = mx + b </md> where <md> m = \frac{S_{XY}}{S_{XX}} \ \text{and} \ b = \bar{y} - m\bar{x}. </md> 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <example>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Activity 16 problem 2c-2e
            </p>
        </statement>
    </example>

</section>
